### 2. **`MainActivity.kt` (Main Activity File)**

This is the Kotlin code for the MainActivity that implements the button functionalities.

```kotlin
package com.example.mypreferenceapp

import android.content.Intent
import android.media.MediaPlayer
import android.net.Uri
import android.os.Bundle
import android.widget.Button
import android.widget.EditText
import android.widget.Toast
import androidx.appcompat.app.AlertDialog
import androidx.appcompat.app.AppCompatActivity

class MainActivity : AppCompatActivity() {

    override fun onCreate(savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {
        super.onCreate(savedInstanceState)
        setContentView(R.layout.activity_main)

        // Show dialog on button click
        findViewById<Button>(R.id.btnDialog).setOnClickListener {
            AlertDialog.Builder(this)
                .setTitle("Info")
                .setMessage("This is a dialog box.")
                .setPositiveButton("OK", null)
                .show()
        }

        // SharedPreferences
        val prefs = getSharedPreferences("mypref", MODE_PRIVATE)

        // Save to SharedPreferences on button click
        findViewById<Button>(R.id.btnSavePref).setOnClickListener {
            val name = findViewById<EditText>(R.id.etName).text.toString()
            prefs.edit().putString("userName", name).apply()
            Toast.makeText(this, "Saved in SharedPreferences", Toast.LENGTH_SHORT).show()
        }

        // Send SMS
        findViewById<Button>(R.id.sms).setOnClickListener {
            startActivity(Intent(Intent.ACTION_VIEW, Uri.parse("smsto:12345")).putExtra("sms_body", "Hello"))
        }

        // Open Website
        findViewById<Button>(R.id.web).setOnClickListener {
            startActivity(Intent(Intent.ACTION_VIEW, Uri.parse("https://google.com")))
        }

        // Play Audio
        findViewById<Button>(R.id.audio).setOnClickListener {
            MediaPlayer.create(this, R.raw.sample_audio).start()
        }
    }
}
```

### 3. **`AndroidManifest.xml` (Manifest File)**

This is the manifest file that defines the app and its permissions.

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    package="com.example.mypreferenceapp">

    <application
        android:allowBackup="true"
        android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
        android:label="@string/app_name"
        android:theme="@style/Theme.MyPreferenceApp">
        <activity android:name=".MainActivity">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>
    </application>

</manifest>
```

### 4. **Adding an Audio File**

Make sure to add an audio file (`sample_audio.mp3`) to the `res/raw` folder. If the `raw` folder doesn't exist, create it under `res/`:

```
res/
   raw/
       sample_audio.mp3
```

If you don't have an audio file, you can download any `.mp3` file and rename it to `sample_audio.mp3` or use any file you prefer.

### Running the Application:

1. **Ensure that your Android device or emulator is connected**.
2. **Open the project in Android Studio**.
3. **Build and run** the project on your emulator/device.
4. **Test the functionality**:

   * **Show Dialog**: Click the "Show Dialog" button to see the dialog box.
   * **Save to SharedPreferences**: Enter a name in the `EditText` and click the "Save to SharedPreferences" button to save the name.
   * **Send SMS**: Click the "Send SMS" button to open the SMS app with a pre-filled message.
   * **Open Website**: Click the "Open Website" button to open a webpage (Google).
   * **Play Audio**: Click the "Play Audio" button to play the audio file (`sample_audio.mp3`).

### Permissions:

For sending SMS or accessing certain features, make sure the relevant permissions are added to the `AndroidManifest.xml`. If you intend to send SMS or use other sensitive features, you might need to request permissions.

For SMS, add this in the `AndroidManifest.xml`:

```xml
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.SEND_SMS"/>
```

If you're targeting **Android 6.0 (API level 23)** or higher, you may also need to request permissions at runtime for SMS and other sensitive operations.

